Dialogue:  0,0:00:07.00,0:00:11.41,Narration,,0,0,0,,In the Universal Century, not every mobile suit gets to be the hero's machine.
Dialogue:  0,0:00:16.50,0:00:23.44,Narration,,0,0,0,,R-X zero N, the Banshee Norn, Goddess of Fate:\Nthe Earth Federation's second answer to the riddle of the Unicorn.
Dialogue:  0,0:00:28.50,0:00:33.47,Narration,,0,0,0,,Like the Unicorn, she carries a psycho-frame,\Narmor that answers a Newtype's will.
Dialogue:  0,0:00:38.50,0:00:46.18,Narration,,0,0,0,,When the N-T-D system awakens, the mask splits, the frame burns green,\Nand a machine of order starts to look disturbingly alive.
Dialogue:  0,0:00:51.00,0:00:57.28,Narration,,0,0,0,,Her pilot is no chosen one. Riddhe Marcenas,\Na Federation ace, fighting for duty rather than destiny.
Dialogue:  0,0:01:02.00,0:01:06.44,Narration,,0,0,0,,While Banagher rides the Unicorn toward answers,\NRiddhe is ordered to silence them.
Dialogue:  0,0:01:11.50,0:01:19.84,Narration,,0,0,0,,The two machines were built as sisters. In the dark of space\Nthey do not simply fight: the Unicorn and the Banshee are pulling on each other.
Dialogue:  0,0:01:24.50,0:01:28.54,Narration,,0,0,0,,And when the psycho-frame screams, it is not a curse. It was a prayer.
Dialogue:  0,0:01:33.00,0:01:39.58,Narration,,0,0,0,,Near the end, sensors report resonance beyond every measurable limit,\Nas if countless hearts were sounding at once.
Dialogue:  0,0:01:43.50,0:01:45.91,Narration,,0,0,0,,She was built to bury the secret of Laplace.
Dialogue:  0,0:01:50.50,0:01:56.87,Narration,,0,0,0,,In the end, even the Federation's sharpest spear\Ncould not stop the truth being born. We were blessed when we were born.
Dialogue:  0,0:01:59.50,0:02:03.15,Narration,,0,0,0,,The Banshee Norn: the reluctant angel of the Universal Century.
